If we don't use $A_{min}$ as a top mochi, it might be used as a bottom mochi. However, since $A_{min}$ is the smallest, it is the hardest to satisfy the condition $A_{top} \le B_{bottom}/2$ if it is the top. Wait, actually, $A_{min}$ is the easiest to satisfy if it is the top because it is small. If it is the bottom, it is the hardest to satisfy because $B_{bottom}/2$ would be small.
So, $A_{min}$ is a very good candidate for the top of a pair.
If we use $A_{min}$ as a top, we need to find a bottom $B$ such that $A_{min} \le B/2$. To save larger mochi for other potential top mochi (which might be larger than $A_{min}$), we should pick the smallest possible $B$ that satisfies the condition.
